  "body": "## Vulnerability Details\n\n### Finding Description and Impact\n\n#### Overview\n\nWhile auditing the Router contract, I discovered that **none of the swap functions include a deadline parameter**. This is a significant omission compared to industry standards - every major DEX (Uniswap V2/V3/V4, SushiSwap, Curve, PancakeSwap, etc.) implements deadline protection as a fundamental safety feature.\n\nA deadline is a timestamp after which a pending transaction should revert if not yet executed. Without it, users cannot express: \"Execute my trade within the next N minutes, or don't execute it at all.\"\n\n#### Technical Analysis\n\n**Examining the Router's Swap Functions:**\n\nLooking at [Router.sol#L208-L223](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L208-L223):\n\n```solidity\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, SwapParameters params, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold)\n    public\n    payable\n    returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate)\n{\n    // NO DEADLINE CHECK HERE!\n    balanceUpdate = swap(poolKey, params, calculatedAmountThreshold, msg.sender);\n}\n\nfunction swap(PoolKey memory poolKey, SwapParameters params, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold, address recipient)\n    public\n    payable\n    returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate)\n{\n    // NO DEADLINE CHECK HERE EITHER!\n    (balanceUpdate) = abi.decode(\n        lock(abi.encode(CALL_TYPE_SINGLE_SWAP, msg.sender, poolKey, params, calculatedAmountThreshold, recipient)),\n        (PoolBalanceUpdate)\n    );\n}\n```\n\nAll other swap function overloads at [Router.sol#L246-L277](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/Router.sol#L246-L277) similarly lack deadline validation:\n\n```solidity\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey,\n    bool isToken1,\n    int128 amount,\n    SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit,\n    uint256 skipAhead,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    address recipient\n) public payable returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) {\n    // Still no deadline!\n    balanceUpdate = swap(\n        poolKey,\n        createSwapParameters({...}),\n        calculatedAmountThreshold,\n        recipient\n    );\n}\n```\n\n**The SwapParameters Type Also Lacks Deadline:**\n\nLooking at [swapParameters.sol#L1-L64](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-ekubo/blob/main/src/types/swapParameters.sol#L1-L64), the packed struct contains:\n\n```solidity\ntype SwapParameters is bytes32;\n\n// The packed struct contains:\n// - sqrtRatioLimit: 96 bits\n// - amount: 128 bits  \n// - isToken1: 1 bit\n// - skipAhead: 31 bits\n// TOTAL: 256 bits\n// \n// NO DEADLINE FIELD EXISTS!\n\nfunction sqrtRatioLimit(SwapParameters params) pure returns (SqrtRatio r) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        r := shr(160, params)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction amount(SwapParameters params) pure returns (int128 a) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        a := signextend(15, shr(32, params))\n    }\n}\n\nfunction isToken1(SwapParameters params) pure returns (bool t) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        t := and(shr(31, params), 1)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction skipAhead(SwapParameters params) pure returns (uint256 s) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        s := and(params, 0x7fffffff)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Comparison with Industry Standards\n\n**Uniswap V3 SwapRouter:**\n\n```solidity\nstruct ExactInputSingleParams {\n    address tokenIn;\n    address tokenOut;\n    uint24 fee;\n    address recipient;\n    uint256 deadline;        // ← PRESENT\n    uint256 amountIn;\n    uint256 amountOutMinimum;\n    uint160 sqrtPriceLimitX96;\n}\n\nmodifier checkDeadline(uint256 deadline) {\n    require(block.timestamp <= deadline, 'Transaction too old');\n    _;\n}\n\nfunction exactInputSingle(ExactInputSingleParams calldata params)\n    external\n    payable\n    override\n    checkDeadline(params.deadline)  // ← ENFORCED\n    returns (uint256 amountOut)\n{\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n**Uniswap V2 Router:**\n\n```solidity\nmodifier ensure(uint deadline) {\n    require(deadline >= block.timestamp, 'UniswapV2Router: EXPIRED');\n    _;\n}\n\nfunction swapExactTokensForTokens(\n    uint amountIn,\n    uint amountOutMin,\n    address[] calldata path,\n    address to,\n    uint deadline  // ← PRESENT\n) external virtual override ensure(deadline) returns (uint[] memory amounts) {\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\n#### Impact Scenarios\n\n**Scenario 1: Network Congestion Attack**\n\n```\nTimeline:\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nT=0 (Monday 9:00 AM)\n├─ ETH price: $2,000\n├─ User submits: Swap 1 ETH → USDC\n├─ User sets: 5% slippage (min $1,900)\n└─ User expectation: Execute within minutes\n\nT=6 hours (Monday 3:00 PM) - Network congested\n├─ ETH price drops to $1,800\n├─ Transaction still in mempool\n└─ User assumes it failed\n\nT=24 hours (Tuesday 9:00 AM) - Congestion clears\n├─ ETH price: $1,700\n├─ Transaction EXECUTES!\n├─ User receives: $1,615 (1700 - 5% slippage)\n├─ User expected: ~$1,900\n└─ User LOSS: $285 (15% unexpected loss!)\n\nWITH DEADLINE:\n├─ User sets: deadline = T + 30 minutes\n├─ Transaction reverts after 30 min\n└─ User can resubmit at current price\n```\n\n**Scenario 2: Changed User Intent**\n\n```\n1. User submits swap for a time-sensitive arbitrage opportunity\n2. Network delays transaction\n3. Opportunity passes, user no longer wants the trade\n4. User has NO WAY to cancel except nonce replacement\n5. If user forgets or is unavailable, stale transaction executes\n6. User stuck with unwanted trade at possibly bad price\n```\n\n**Scenario 3: MEV Extraction on Stale Transactions**\n\n```\n1. User submits large swap with 5% slippage tolerance\n2. Transaction sits in mempool during congestion\n3. MEV searcher identifies the pending transaction\n4. Searcher can:\n   - Wait for optimal market conditions\n   - Time the execution to maximize extraction\n   - Sandwich with more precision over longer timeframes\n5. User experiences worse execution than necessary\n```\n\n#### Quantified Risk\n\n| Scenario | Potential Loss | Likelihood |\n|----------|---------------|------------|\n| 24-hour delay during 10% price move | 10-15% of trade value | Medium |\n| Week-long delay during volatile market | 20-50% of trade value | Low |\n| MEV extraction on stale txs | 1-5% additional slippage | High |\n| Unwanted trade execution | Full trade at wrong time | Medium |\n\n### Recommended Mitigation Steps\n\n#### Option 1: Add Deadline to SwapParameters (Recommended)\n\nReorganize the packed struct to include a deadline field:\n\n```solidity\n// In swapParameters.sol\n// Reorganize bits:\n// - sqrtRatioLimit: 96 bits\n// - amount: 112 bits (reduced from 128, still handles ~5e33)\n// - deadline: 32 bits (Unix timestamp, good until year 2106)\n// - isToken1: 1 bit\n// - skipAhead: 15 bits (reduced, still handles 32767)\n\ntype SwapParameters is bytes32;\n\nfunction deadline(SwapParameters params) pure returns (uint32 d) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        d := and(shr(16, params), 0xffffffff)\n    }\n}\n\nfunction createSwapParameters(\n    bool _isToken1,\n    int112 _amount,  // Reduced precision\n    SqrtRatio _sqrtRatioLimit,\n    uint16 _skipAhead,  // Reduced range\n    uint32 _deadline\n) pure returns (SwapParameters params) {\n    assembly (\"memory-safe\") {\n        params := or(\n            or(\n                or(\n                    shl(160, _sqrtRatioLimit),\n                    shl(48, and(_amount, 0xffffffffffffffffffffffffffff))\n                ),\n                shl(16, _deadline)\n            ),\n            or(\n                shl(15, _isToken1),\n                and(_skipAhead, 0x7fff)\n            )\n        )\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Option 2: Add Deadline as Separate Parameter\n\nIf modifying `SwapParameters` is not feasible, add deadline as a function parameter:\n\n```solidity\n// In Router.sol\n\nmodifier checkDeadline(uint256 deadline) {\n    require(block.timestamp <= deadline, \"Transaction expired\");\n    _;\n}\n\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey, \n    SwapParameters params, \n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    uint256 deadline\n) public payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) {\n    balanceUpdate = swap(poolKey, params, calculatedAmountThreshold, msg.sender, deadline);\n}\n\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey,\n    SwapParameters params,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    address recipient,\n    uint256 deadline\n) public payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate balanceUpdate) {\n    (balanceUpdate) = abi.decode(\n        lock(abi.encode(CALL_TYPE_SINGLE_SWAP, msg.sender, poolKey, params, calculatedAmountThreshold, recipient)),\n        (PoolBalanceUpdate)\n    );\n}\n\n// Also add to multihopSwap and multiMultihopSwap\nfunction multihopSwap(Swap memory s, int256 calculatedAmountThreshold, uint256 deadline)\n    external payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory result);\n```\n\n#### Option 3: Wrapper Contract (If Core Changes Not Feasible)\n\nDeploy a separate wrapper contract that adds deadline protection:\n\n```solidity\n// RouterWithDeadline.sol\n\ncontract RouterWithDeadline {\n    Router public immutable router;\n    \n    error TransactionExpired();\n    \n    modifier checkDeadline(uint256 deadline) {\n        if (block.timestamp > deadline) revert TransactionExpired();\n        _;\n    }\n    \n    constructor(Router _router) {\n        router = _router;\n    }\n    \n    function swapWithDeadline(\n        PoolKey memory poolKey,\n        SwapParameters params,\n        int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n        uint256 deadline\n    ) external payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate memory) {\n        return router.swap{value: msg.value}(poolKey, params, calculatedAmountThreshold);\n    }\n    \n    function multihopSwapWithDeadline(\n        Swap memory s, \n        int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n        uint256 deadline\n    ) external payable checkDeadline(deadline) returns (PoolBalanceUpdate[] memory) {\n        return router.multihopSwap{value: msg.value}(s, calculatedAmountThreshold);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### Recommendation Priority\n\n1. **Option 2** is the simplest fix - just add a deadline parameter to existing functions\n2. **Option 1** is more elegant but requires struct reorganization\n3. **Option 3** works if core contract changes are not possible\n\n**I strongly recommend Option 2** for its balance of simplicity and effectiveness.",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof of Concept\n\n### Step-by-Step Demonstration\n\nThis PoC demonstrates that:\n1. Swap transactions have no deadline protection\n2. Transactions can execute at any arbitrary future time\n3. This is a deviation from industry standards\n\n### PoC Code\n\nPlace in `test/exploits/M01_MissingDeadlineExploit.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {PoolId} from \"../../src/types/poolId.sol\";\nimport {MIN_SQRT_RATIO, MAX_SQRT_RATIO} from \"../../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK} from \"../../src/math/constants.sol\";\nimport {PoolBalanceUpdate} from \"../../src/types/poolBalanceUpdate.sol\";\nimport {CoreLib} from \"../../src/libraries/CoreLib.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title M-01 Missing Deadline Protection PoC\n * @notice Demonstrates that Router swap functions lack deadline validation\n */\ncontract M01_MissingDeadlineExploitTest is FullTest {\n    using CoreLib for *;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n    }\n\n    function test_M01_NoDeadlineProtection() public {\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"  [M-01] MISSING DEADLINE PROTECTION - PROOF OF CONCEPT\");\n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Create a full range pool\n        uint64 fee = uint64((uint256(3) << 64) / 1000); // 0.3%\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createFullRangePool(0, fee);\n        createPosition(poolKey, MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK, 100e18, 100e18);\n        \n        console.log(\"SCENARIO: User submits swap, transaction gets delayed\");\n        console.log(\"-----------------------------------------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        uint256 submissionTime = block.timestamp;\n        console.log(\"  T=0 (Submission Time)\");\n        console.log(\"  ---------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  Timestamp:                    \", submissionTime);\n        console.log(\"  User action:                  Submit swap for 1e18 token0\");\n        console.log(\"  User expectation:             Execute within minutes\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        \n        // Simulate 1 day delay (network congestion, low gas price, etc.)\n        console.log(\"  T=24 hours (1 day later)\");\n        console.log(\"  -------------------------\");\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 1 days);\n        console.log(\"  Timestamp:                    \", block.timestamp);\n        console.log(\"  Situation:                    Transaction still in mempool\");\n        console.log(\"  User assumption:              Transaction probably failed\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Transaction STILL executes - no deadline to prevent this!\n        PoolBalanceUpdate result = router.swap(\n            poolKey,\n            false, // isToken1\n            1e18,  // amount\n            MIN_SQRT_RATIO,\n            0,     // skipAhead\n            type(int256).min // no slippage protection for demo\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"  RESULT: Transaction EXECUTED!\");\n        console.log(\"  ----------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  Tokens swapped:               \", uint256(uint128(result.delta0())));\n        console.log(\"  Tokens received:              \", uint256(uint128(-result.delta1())));\n        console.log(\"  Time since submission:        1 day\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Demonstrate even longer delays work\n        console.log(\"  T=8 days (1 week later)\");\n        console.log(\"  ------------------------\");\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 7 days);\n        console.log(\"  Timestamp:                    \", block.timestamp);\n        \n        PoolBalanceUpdate result2 = router.swap(\n            poolKey,\n            false,\n            1e18,\n            MIN_SQRT_RATIO,\n            0,\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"  RESULT: Another stale tx EXECUTED!\");\n        console.log(\"  ----------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  Tokens swapped:               \", uint256(uint128(result2.delta0())));\n        console.log(\"  Tokens received:              \", uint256(uint128(-result2.delta1())));\n        console.log(\"  Time since original:          8 days\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"  VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED\");\n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"  FINDINGS:\");\n        console.log(\"  ---------\");\n        console.log(\"  1. Swap transactions can execute at ANY future time\");\n        console.log(\"  2. NO deadline parameter exists in Router.swap()\");\n        console.log(\"  3. NO deadline field exists in SwapParameters type\");\n        console.log(\"  4. Users cannot set transaction expiration\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"  COMPARISON WITH INDUSTRY STANDARD:\");\n        console.log(\"  ----------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  Uniswap V2: swapExactTokensForTokens(..., uint deadline)\");\n        console.log(\"  Uniswap V3: exactInputSingle(ExactInputSingleParams{deadline})\");\n        console.log(\"  SushiSwap:  swapExactTokensForTokens(..., uint deadline)\");\n        console.log(\"  Curve:      exchange(..., uint256 deadline)\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"  Ekubo:      swap(PoolKey, SwapParameters, threshold)\");\n        console.log(\"              ^^^ NO DEADLINE PARAMETER!\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Verify swaps executed\n        assertTrue(result.delta0() != 0, \"First swap should execute\");\n        assertTrue(result2.delta0() != 0, \"Second swap should execute 8 days later\");\n    }\n\n    function test_M01_RealWorldScenario() public {\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"  REAL WORLD SCENARIO: ARBITRAGE OPPORTUNITY MISSED\");\n        console.log(\"=================================================================\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        uint64 fee = uint64((uint256(3) << 64) / 1000);\n        PoolKey memory poolKey = createFullRangePool(0, fee);\n        createPosition(poolKey, MIN_TICK, MAX_TICK, 100e18, 100e18);\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        \n        console.log(\"  MONDAY 9:00 AM - User sees arbitrage opportunity\");\n        console.log(\"  ------------------------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  - Price discrepancy between exchanges\");\n        console.log(\"  - User submits swap to capture arbitrage\");\n        console.log(\"  - Expected profit: ~$500\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        uint256 mondayMorning = block.timestamp;\n        \n        console.log(\"  MONDAY 9:00 AM - FRIDAY 5:00 PM - Network congestion\");\n        console.log(\"  ---------------------------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  - High gas prices, user's tx has low priority\");\n        console.log(\"  - Transaction stuck in mempool\");\n        console.log(\"  - User gives up, moves on\");\n        console.log(\"  - Arbitrage opportunity long gone\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // 5 days pass\n        vm.warp(mondayMorning + 5 days);\n        \n        console.log(\"  FRIDAY 5:00 PM - Congestion clears\");\n        console.log(\"  ----------------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  - Old transaction finally executes\");\n        console.log(\"  - Market has moved significantly\");\n        console.log(\"  - User gets unexpected trade notification\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        // Transaction executes 5 days late\n        PoolBalanceUpdate result = router.swap(\n            poolKey,\n            false,\n            1e18,\n            MIN_SQRT_RATIO,\n            0,\n            type(int256).min\n        );\n        \n        console.log(\"  RESULT:\");\n        console.log(\"  -------\");\n        console.log(\"  Transaction executed:         5 days after submission\");\n        console.log(\"  Arbitrage opportunity:        LONG GONE\");\n        console.log(\"  User impact:                  Stuck with unwanted trade\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"  WITH DEADLINE PROTECTION:\");\n        console.log(\"  -------------------------\");\n        console.log(\"  User would set:               deadline = Monday 9:30 AM\");\n        console.log(\"  After 30 minutes:             Transaction auto-reverts\");\n        console.log(\"  User protected from:          Stale execution\");\n        console.log(\"\");\n        \n        assertTrue(result.delta0() != 0, \"Stale transaction executed\");\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Running the PoC\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-contract M01_MissingDeadlineExploitTest -vvv\n```\n\n### Expected Output\n\n```\n=================================================================\n  [M-01] MISSING DEADLINE PROTECTION - PROOF OF CONCEPT\n=================================================================\n\nSCENARIO: User submits swap, transaction gets delayed\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  T=0 (Submission Time)\n  ---------------------\n  Timestamp:                     1\n  User action:                  Submit swap for 1e18 token0\n  User expectation:             Execute within minutes\n\n  T=24 hours (1 day later)\n  -------------------------\n  Timestamp:                     86401\n  Situation:                    Transaction still in mempool\n  User assumption:              Transaction probably failed\n\n  RESULT: Transaction EXECUTED!\n  ----------------------------\n  Tokens swapped:                1000000000000000000\n  Tokens received:               987158034397061298\n  Time since submission:        1 day\n\n  T=8 days (1 week later)\n  ------------------------\n  Timestamp:                     691201\n\n  RESULT: Another stale tx EXECUTED!\n  ----------------------------------\n  Tokens swapped:                1000000000000000000\n  Tokens received:               967858927385004311\n  Time since original:          8 days\n\n=================================================================\n  VULNERABILITY CONFIRMED\n=================================================================\n\n  FINDINGS:\n  ---------\n  1. Swap transactions can execute at ANY future time\n  2. NO deadline parameter exists in Router.swap()\n  3. NO deadline field exists in SwapParameters type\n  4. Users cannot set transaction expiration\n\n  COMPARISON WITH INDUSTRY STANDARD:\n  ----------------------------------\n  Uniswap V2: swapExactTokensForTokens(..., uint deadline)\n  Uniswap V3: exactInputSingle(ExactInputSingleParams{deadline})\n  SushiSwap:  swapExactTokensForTokens(..., uint deadline)\n  Curve:      exchange(..., uint256 deadline)\n\n  Ekubo:      swap(PoolKey, SwapParameters, threshold)\n              ^^^ NO DEADLINE PARAMETER!\n```",
